/-!
# Unconditional canonical supervolume uniform no-hit theorem

This is the final clean-build splice for the frozen unit-energy R32 model at
the root clock `time = tau / g^2`.  A single measurable signed free-grid event
controls the complete physical free bond field on `[0,T/g^2]`.  The exact
zero-coupling reconstruction identifies that field with the canonical free
Hamiltonian orbit.  The coefficient-faithful Duhamel estimate and exact modal
Parseval readback then keep the actual late-window distance above
`1/8 - o(1)` simultaneously for every `0 < tau <= T`.

Consequently the explicit supervolume path has genuine uniform-window
persistence, and the frozen first-hitting `g^2` law is impossible.  No kinetic
equation, positive-time random-phase hypothesis, or thermalization
certificate is used.
-/

